    "answer": {
      "short": "$p=0.3,\\ q=0.1$",
      "worked": "The probabilities sum to $1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}p+0.25+0.35+q&=1\\\\p+q&=0.4\\qquad(1)\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $E(X)=\\sum xP(x)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3p+7(0.25)+8(0.35)+9q&=6.35\\\\3p+9q&=1.8\\qquad(2)\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract $3\\times(1)$ from $(2)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}6q&=0.6\\\\q&=0.1\\\\p&=0.4-0.1\\\\p&=0.3\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
